                    }
                ],
                "description": "In Tamil, consonants are called மெய் எழுத்துகள் (Mei Ezhuthukal). These are the body sounds of the language that cannot be pronounced independently without a vowel sound. Tamil has 18 pure consonants: க், ங், ச், ஞ், ட், ண், த், ந், ப், ம், ய், ர், ல், வ், ழ், ள், ற், ன். When combined with vowels, they form composite letters (உயிர்மெய் எழுத்துகள்). These consonants are organized into different groups based on their place of articulation in the mouth."
